.TH CHARON 1
.SH NAME
charon \- web browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm/charon
[
.B -h
]
[
.B -m
.I mountpoint
]
[
.B -g
.IB w x h
]
[
.I url
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Charon
shows web pages: HTML as the WHATWG standard parses it, styled by CSS
(selectors level 4, the cascade with layers, custom properties,
.BR calc() ,
media and feature queries, colour level 4) and laid out by block, inline,
float, positioned, flex, grid and table formatting.
Text is set in TrueType faces (DejaVu) at any size, weight and slant;
images may be PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP, AVIF or SVG.
A page's scripts run when the
.B scripts
setting is
.B on
(it is
.B off
by default; the setting is a line of the user's
.BR lib/charon/settings ,
as Charon's other engine settings are).
Each page's scripts run in a realm of their own (see
.IR js (1)),
on a process confined to a namespace holding only the network and, for a
.B file:
page, its directory; the document they change is the one shown.
A script that runs thirty seconds is stopped.
.PP
The window is a location bar with back, forward and reload (stop, while
loading) buttons, the page, and a status line that shows the URL of the
link under the pointer.
Form controls are Tk widgets placed over the page; typing in them changes
the document.
.PP
Keys, when the page has the focus:
.TF Alt-Left
.PD
.TP
.B "Up Down PgUp PgDn space Home End"
scroll
.TP
.B "Backspace Left Right"
back, forward
.TP
.B Ctrl-L
edit the location
.TP
.B Ctrl-F
find (Ctrl-G finds the next)
.TP
.B Ctrl-R
reload
.TP
.B Escape
stop
.TP
.B Ctrl-Q
quit
.PD
.PP
Button 1 follows a link or works a control; button 3 is a menu.
.PP
A location without a scheme is taken as
.B https://
unless it begins with
.BR / ,
which is a file.
.SS Files
Charon serves its session, at
.I mountpoint
(default
.BR /mnt/charon )
in its own name space, and posts it as
.B #scharon/fs
for any other name space of the same user:
.IP
.EX
mount -A '#scharon/fs' /mnt/charon
.EE
.PP
The tree:
.TF forms
.PD
.TP
.B ctl
Commands:
.BI open " url"\f1,
.BR back ,
.BR forward ,
.BR reload ,
.BR stop ,
.BI follow " n"\f1,
.BI click " node"\f1,
.BI set " node value"\f1,
.BI submit " form" " \fR[\fPnode\fR]\fP"\f1,
.BI size " w" x h\f1,
.BI width " w"\f1,
.BI scroll " y"\f1.
.TP
.B url
.br
.ns
.TP
.B title
.br
.ns
.TP
.B status
.BI loading " url"\f1,
.BR done ,
or
.BI error " message"\f1.
.TP
.B text
The page's rendered text in reading order, one block per line, table
cells separated by tabs.
.TP
.B links
.IR n " " url " " text
per link.
.TP
.B forms
.IR form " " node " " kind " " name " " value
per control, with
.B checked
appended to a checked box; a select's options follow it on lines
beginning with a tab.
.TP
.B find
Write text; read the lines of
.B text
that contain it, ignoring case.
.TP
.B image
The viewport, as an
.IR image (6).
.TP
.B event
Each read waits for the next of the events since the file was opened:
.BI loading " url"\f1,
.BI done " url"\f1,
.BI error " message"\f1,
.BR stopped ,
.B update
(a form control changed).
To wait for a navigation, open
.B event
before writing
.BR ctl .
.TP
.BI dom/ n /
Node
.IR n :
.B tag
.RB ( #text
for text),
.B attrs
(name and value per line),
.BR text ,
.B style
(the computed style, a property and value per line),
.B box
(each box it generated, as
.IR kind " " x " " y " " w " " h
in page coordinates) and
.B children
(their node numbers).
.PD
.PP
A file's contents are taken when it is opened.
.PP
With
.BR -h ,
there is no window: only the files.
.PP
Charon fetches
.B http
and
.B https
only through
.IR webfs (4)
at
.BR /mnt/web ,
starting one if none is mounted, so what it can reach, and with which
cookies, is that mount.
.SS Xenith
A browser window in Xenith (a URL opened there) is the same session,
served the same way: each window's page is posted as
.BI #sxenith/ id
.RI ( id
the window's), and the window's file
.B web
names it:
.IP
.EX
mount -A `{cat /mnt/xenith/7/web} /n/page
.EE
.PP
A page loaded, a field set or a form submitted through the files shows
in the window.  The posted file goes when the window closes.
.SH EXAMPLE
Drive the window from a shell:
.IP
.EX
; mount -A '#scharon/fs' /mnt/charon
; echo open https://example.org/ >/mnt/charon/ctl
; cat /mnt/charon/title
; grep ' search ' /mnt/charon/forms
1 31 search q
; echo set 31 inferno >/mnt/charon/ctl
; echo submit 1 >/mnt/charon/ctl
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/charon/charon.b
.br
.B /appl/lib/web
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR webfs (4),
.B /docs/XEN.md
(Xenith's browser windows),
.B /docs/CHARON-ENGINE.md
.SH BUGS
No frames, text selection, bookmarks or HTTP cache yet.
Scripts' storage and cookies last as long as the page; shadow DOM is
not shown; there is no canvas, media or workers.
